      "gate": "G5",
      "claim": "NEGATIVE CONTROL, which bean m015 asks for explicitly -- AND A CORRECTION TO WHAT IT PROVES. The trefoil 3_1 is a TORUS knot, Seifert fibred, not hyperbolic. It is NOT the case that the gluing equations have no solution for it: the flat shapes (-1, 2) are RATIONAL and satisfy all four equations EXACTLY, verified here. What fails is POSITIVITY -- every shape is real, so every tetrahedron is flat, every Bloch-Wigner term is 0, and the volume is 0. So the gluing equations ALONE DO NOT DETECT HYPERBOLICITY; the condition Im(z_j) > 0 does. That is what this control actually establishes, and it is a sharper statement than 'no solution'",
